pt":"assets","tag":"Assets","value":"1577741000","accn":"0001336917-14-000008","filed":"2014-02-21"},{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2013-12-31","concept":"current_liabilities","tag":"LiabilitiesCurrent","value":"426630000","accn":"0001336917-14-000008","filed":"2014-02-21"},{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2013-12-31","concept":"lt_debt","tag":"LongTermDebtNoncurrent","value":"47951000","accn":"0001336917-14-000008","filed":"2014-02-21"}]},"company":{"attrs":{"cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2013-12-31","activeRevision":"7d3e957400e5","liveRevision":""}},"filings":[{"attrs":{"accn":"0001336917-13-000011","filed":"2013-02-25","cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1336917/000133691713000011/0001336917-13-000011-index.htm","form":"10-K"}},{"attrs":{"accn":"0001336917-14-000008","filed":"2014-02-21","cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1336917/000133691714000008/ua-20131231x10k.htm","form":"10-K"}}],"findings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":0,"findingIndex":1,"management_says":"No explicit explanation provided in the evidence pack for the rise in receivables or the decline in operating cash flow.","numbers_show":"Receivables grew slower than revenue (19.6% vs 27.1%) and DSO improved annually, consistent with a DTC mix shift. However, quarterly signals show Q1 receivables outpacing revenue (+25.4% vs +22.7%) and DSO rising, while Q4 shows the opposite. The 40% CFO decline amid rising income and better DSO indicates large adverse working-capital moves (e.g., inventory, payables, accruals) not discussed.","fit":"unverified","evidence":["E25","E27","E28","E29","E30","E26","E31"],"verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"findingIndex":3,"management_says":"Beneish M-score of -1.7072 (flagged above -1.78 threshold) indicates potential earnings manipulation risk.","numbers_show":"The M-score components show high AQI (2.27) and SGI (1.27), driven by asset quality and sales growth. This signal does not directly contradict the revenue growth explanation but warrants scrutiny of accruals.","fit":"unverified","evidence":["E31"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}}],"rulings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":0,"rulingIndex":1,"finding_index":1,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Management provides no explicit explanation for the 40% decline in operating cash flow (E26) despite rising net income and improved annual DSO (E25). The defender's explanation (working-capital investment) relies on facts not in the evidence pack (inventory, payables, accruals). Quarterly DSO patterns (E27-E30) show seasonal variation but do not quantify the cash-flow impact. Since the explanation rests on facts outside the pack, it is unverified.","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29","E30","E31"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":1,"innocent_explanation":"The 40% CFO decline ($199.8M to $120.1M, E26) reflects substantial working-capital investment — inventory build, higher payables, and accrued expenses — to support 27% revenue growth, which is not itemized in the evidence pack. The quarterly DSO pattern (E27-E30) shows a Q1 receivables build (DSO 46→48 days) that reverses by Q4 (DSO 32→28 days), consistent with seasonal shipment timing rather than systemic collection issues. Annual DSO improved (35→33 days, E25), indicating overall collection efficiency.","evidence":["E26","E25","E27","E28","E29","E30"],"support":"outside the pack"},"final_verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers","confidence":0.82}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":3,"finding_index":3,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"The Beneish M-score of -1.7072 flags potential manipulation risk, but the high AQI (2.27) and SGI (1.27) are driven by legitimate high sales growth (27.1%) and asset growth (36.3%). The numbers do not distinguish between manipulation and high growth.","evidence":["E31","E1","E13","E10","E22"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":3,"innocent_explanation":"The Beneish M-score of -1.7072 (flagged above -1.78) is driven by high sales growth (SGI=1.27) and asset growth (AQI=2.27) from legitimate business expansion, not earnings manipulation; revenue grew 27.1% and total assets grew 36.3% year-over-year.","evidence":["E31","E1","E13","E10","E22"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.8}}],"audit":[{"seq":31,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":141,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":142,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"filing:accn:0001336917-13-000011 -[supports]-> evidence:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31","kind":"relate"},{"seq":143,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"filing:accn:0001336917-14-000008 -[supports]-> evidence:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31","kind":"relate"},{"seq":212,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31 -[supports]-> finding:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:s0:f1","kind":"relate"},{"seq":236,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31 -[cites]-> ruling:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:s0:r1","kind":"relate"},{"seq":353,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31 -[supports]-> finding:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:s2:f3","kind":"relate"},{"seq":395,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E31 -[cites]-> ruling:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:s2:r3","kind":"relate"}]}